   "text": {
    "L1": "Co-prime describes a pair of numbers, not just one number.",
    "L2": "Two numbers are co-prime when their only common factor is 1.",
    "L3": "Being prime is about one number. Co-prime is about what two numbers share.",
    "L4": "Here is the myth: both numbers must be prime. That is not true.",
    "L5": "Fourteen has factors 1, 2, 7 and 14. Twenty-five has factors 1, 5 and 25.",
    "L6": "Their only common factor is 1, so 14 and 25 are co-prime, although neither is prime.",
    "L7": "To decide, list factors for both numbers and look for a shared factor besides 1."
   },
